### Quick Troubleshooting Reference

| Error | Likely cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `credssp` / NLA error | NLA required, wrong security layer | Try `/sec:rdp` then `/sec:tls` |
| Immediate disconnect | rdesktop + modern Windows | Switch to xfreerdp |
| `certificate error` | Self-signed cert on lab box | Add `/cert:ignore` |
| `connection refused` | RDP not enabled or wrong port | Confirm port 3389 open with nmap |
| `account restricted` | User not in Remote Desktop Users | Check group membership |
| Black screen after login | Display resolution issue | Add `/dynamic-resolution` or `/size:1280x720` |
| Pass-the-Hash fails | Restricted Admin mode disabled | Enable via registry or use evil-winrm instead |

---

> **Most reliable combination for OSCP lab boxes:**
> `xfreerdp /v:$IP /u:username /p:'password' /d:corp.local /cert:ignore`
> Those two flags (`/cert:ignore` and `/d:`) alone resolve the majority of connection failures.
